course: dictionary
lesson: 14528
title: Who did it? Meet the perpetrator
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A perpetrator is the person who does something wrong or harmful, especially a crime. When you read a news report or a detective story, the perpetrator is the one who did the bad act. «The police caught the perpetrator after a short chase.» The clue is in the words: caught, chase and the bad act, so the perpetrator is the person who did the wrong thing.
explain: The word is a little formal, so you will often meet it in law, news and police reports. «Police are looking for the perpetrators of the robbery.» Here perpetrators is the plural, meaning more than one person. Always ask: who did the harm? That is the perpetrator.
explain: Stories about bullying use the same word. «In the playground story, the perpetrator teased the new girl, and the victim felt sad all day.» The perpetrator is the one who does the harm, and the victim is the one who is harmed. Knowing which is which helps you understand who is to blame and who needs help.
fact: A perpetrator is a person who does something wrong or harmful.
fact: «Perpetrator» is a noun: one perpetrator, many perpetrators.
fact: The word is formal and is often used in law, police reports and news stories.
fact: «Perpetrator» means the person who did the bad act, especially a crime.
fact: In a bullying story, the victim is the person who is harmed, and the perpetrator is the person who causes the harm.
exercise: «The police caught the perpetrator after a short chase.» Who is the perpetrator? | The police officer who chased them | The shop owner who was robbed | *The person who did the wrong thing | The witness who saw it happen
exercise: «Police are looking for the perpetrators of the robbery.» Find and copy the word that means the people who did the robbery. | police | looking | robbery | *perpetrators
exercise: «In the playground story, the perpetrator teased the new girl, and the victim felt sad all day.» Who is the victim? | The child who did the teasing | *The new girl who was teased | The playground supervisor | The teacher who stopped it
test: What does perpetrator mean? | *A person who does something wrong or harmful | A type of new bicycle | A person who helps people feel better | A police station
test: «The perpetrators ran off before the guard arrived.» How many people does perpetrators mean? | *More than one | None at all | Two only | One
exam: «The detective said the perpetrator left a muddy footprint by the back door.» What is the perpetrator? | *The person who did the wrong thing | A footprint in the mud | A detective who looks for clues | The owner of the house
